{
    "background_story": "In the mystical realm of Aethoria, where ancient forests whispered secrets to the wind, Pooka was a gentle erianthus - a creature with the body of a deer and the delicate wings of a butterfly. Her fur shimmered with an ethereal glow, reflecting the colors of the setting sun. Pooka's home was a lush meadow, where she spent her days sipping nectar from rare flowers and listening to the songs of the forest. As the seasons changed, Pooka's wings would adapt, shifting from iridescent blues to vibrant oranges, allowing her to blend seamlessly into her surroundings. With a touch of her wing, she could heal the wounded petals of the erianthus flowers, and her presence was said to bring good fortune to those who sought refuge in the meadow. Pooka's wisdom and kindness earned her the title of Guardian of the Meadow, a role she cherished deeply.",
